 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "Se habla español",
  "alumno": "Spanish is spoken"
 },
 "intro": "With «se» you speak of nobody in particular: signs, rules and customs.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "se habla",
   "significado": "is spoken; people speak",
   "pron": "se A-bla",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The language is the subject: «se habla español», «se hablan dos lenguas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se vende",
   "significado": "is for sale (one thing)",
   "pron": "se BEN-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With one thing: «se vende un piso». With several: «se venden pisos».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se venden",
   "significado": "are for sale (several things)",
   "pron": "se BEN-den",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The final n marks the plural and agrees with what is sold: «se venden coches».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se alquila",
   "significado": "for rent",
   "pron": "se al-KI-la",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The qu sounds like k: al-KI-la. A sign says «se alquila piso».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se puede",
   "significado": "one can; it is allowed",
   "pron": "se PWE-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«¿Se puede?» is used to ask permission. An infinitive follows: «se puede entrar».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se dice que",
   "significado": "people say that",
   "pron": "se DI-the ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It does not say who speaks. A sentence follows «que»: «se dice que va a llover».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "se necesita",
   "significado": "is needed; wanted",
   "pron": "se ne-the-SI-ta",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It appears in job ads: «se necesita camarero». With several: «se necesitan».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "prohibido",
   "significado": "forbidden",
   "pron": "pro-i-BI-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The h is silent: pro-i-BI-do. It is very common on signs: «prohibido fumar».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "aparcar",
   "significado": "to park",
   "pron": "a-par-KAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In many countries of the Americas they say «estacionar». The c sounds like k: a-par-KAR.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "entrada",
   "significado": "ticket; entrance",
   "pron": "en-TRA-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has two meanings: the door and the ticket. The context tells you which.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cartel",
   "significado": "sign; poster",
   "pron": "kar-TEL",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The stress is at the end: kar-TEL. A sign can be in the street or on a door.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "fumar",
   "significado": "to smoke",
   "pron": "fu-MAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a regular -ar verb. On signs: «prohibido fumar», «no se puede fumar».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
