 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nobody in particular",
     "texto": [
      "With **se** you can speak of nobody in particular.\n\n- **Passive with se:** what is sold, rented or spoken is the **subject**, and the verb agrees with it: **Se vende** un piso. **Se venden** pisos.\n- **Impersonal with se:** there is no subject and the verb stays **singular**: Aquí **se come** muy bien. ¿**Se puede** aparcar? **Se dice** que va a llover.\n\nYou will see **Se habla español** on many signs."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The verb with «se»",
     "texto": [
      "Look at what the verb agrees with:\n\n- With a noun after it, **it agrees with the noun**: se vende **un coche**, se venden **coches**; se habla **español**, se hablan **dos lenguas**.\n- With an infinitive or with **que**, the verb is **singular**: se puede **aparcar**, se dice **que** hay una fiesta.\n- With an adverb there is no subject: aquí **se come** bien.\n\nOther ways of speaking in general: **ellos** with no subject («dicen que es bueno») or **tú** («si comes bien, vives mejor»)."
     ],
